प्र-√ वच् P. -वक्ति (inf. -वा॑चे, RV. ix, 95, 2), to proclaim, announce, praise, commend, mention, teach, impart, explain (with acc. of thing and dat. or gen. of person), RV. &c. &c.;
to tell of, betray, TS.;
to give, deliver (with acc. and dat.), RV.; Br.;
to speak, say, tell (with acc., rarely dat. of person, and acc. of thing), PraśnUp.; MBh.; Hariv. &c. ;
to declare to be, call (2 acc.), Śrutab. :
Caus. -वाचयति, to cause to announce, Gobh. :
Desid. -विवक्षति, MBh. xii, 3767 (w.r. -विवक्षतः for -विविक्षतः).

प्र-√ वद् P. Ā. -वदति, ˚ते (Ved. inf. प्र॑-वदितोस्), to speak out, pronounce, proclaim, declare, utter, say, tell, RV. &c. &c.;
to speak to (acc.), Bhaṭṭ.;
to raise the voice (said of birds and animals), R.; Var.;
to roar, splash (said of water), ĀśvGṛ.;
 (cf. अ-प्रवदत्) to assert, affirm, state, ŚvetUp.; Var.;
to pronounce to be, call, name (2 acc.), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to offer for sale (with instr. of price), Pañcat. (v.l.) :
Caus. -वादयति, to cause to sound, play (with acc. of the instrument), ŚāṅkhŚr.; MBh. &c.;
 (without an object) to play, make music, Hariv. (also -वाद्यति, with act. meaning, MBh. xii, 1899).

प्र-√ 5. वस् P. -वसति, (rarely Ā.; e.g. pf. -वासां चक्रे, ChUp.; fut. -वत्स्यति, ĀśvŚr.; ind.p. प्रोष्य, ŚBr.),
to go or sojourn abroad, leave home, depart, RV. &c. &c.;
to disappear vanish, cease, Hariv.;
to stop at a place, abide, dwell, MBh.; R.;
 (= Caus.) to banish to (loc.), R. :
Caus. -वासयति, to make to dwell in Divyāv.;
to order to live abroad, turn out, expel, banish, Mn.; MBh. &c.:
Desid. -विवत्सति, to intend to set out on a journey, Śiś.;
to be about to depart from (abl.), Car.

प्र-√ वह् P. -वहति, (Pāṇ. i, 3, 81), to carry forwards, draw or drag on wards, RV.; AitBr.; ŚrS.; R. ;
to carry off in flowing, wash away, RV.; ĀśvGṛ.; R.;
to lead or bring to (acc.), MBh.; Bhaṭṭ.;
to bear, Bhaṭṭ.;
to exhibit, show, utter, BhP.;
 (Ā.) to drive onwards, RV.;
to flow along, Kathās.; Rājat.;
to rush, blow (as wind), MBh. :
Caus. -वाहयति, to cause to go away, send off, dismiss, ĀśvŚr.;
to cause to swim away (Pass., to be washed away), MārkP.; HPariś.;
to set in motion or on foot, Hariv.; R.

प्र-वि-√ चर् P. -चरति, to go forwards, advance, MBh.; Hit.;
to roam about, Mṛcch.;
to walk or wander through (acc.), MBh. :
Caus. -चारयति See below.

प्र-वि-√ चल् P. -चलति, to become agitated, tremble, quake, MBh.;
to become confused or disturbed, Hariv.;
to deviate or swerve from (abl.), MBh.; Bhartṛ. :
Caus. -चालयति, to cause to tremble, shake, Hariv.

प्र-√ 1. विद् P. -वेत्ति, to know, understand, RV.; AV.; MBh. :
Caus. -वेदयति, ˚ते, to make known, communicate, relate, TUp.; MBh.;
 (P.) to know or understand right, MuṇḍUp.

प्र-√ 3. विद् P. Ā. -विन्दति, ˚ते, to find, find out, invent, RV.;
to anticipate, ŚBr. :
Intens. -वेविदीति, to attain, partake of (acc.), RV.

प्र-वि-√ 1. धा P. Ā. -दधाति, -धत्ते, to place apart, divide, Suśr.;
 (Ā.) to meditate, think upon, R.; Rājat.;
to place in front, put at the head, pay attention to, Śukas.

प्र-वि-√ मुच् P. Ā. -मुञ्चति, ˚ते, to set free, liberate, R.;
to give up, relinquish, abandon, MBh.; Kathās. &c.:
Pass. -मुच्यते, to be freed from or rid of (abl.), Suśr.

प्र-वि-√ ली Ā. or Pass. -लीयते, (˚ति), to become dissolved, melt or vanish away, MuṇḍUp.; MBh. &c.:
Caus. -लापयति, to cause to disappear or dissolve itself into (loc.), Śaṃk.; BhP., Sch.;
to dissolve, melt (trans.), Suśr.

प्र-वि-√ लोक् P. -लोकयति, to look forwards or about, R.;
to perceive, notice, consider, Kathās.;
 (in astron.) to observe, Gol.

प्र-√ विश् P. Ā. -विशति, ˚ते, to enter, go into, resort to (acc. or loc.), RV. &c. &c. (with अग्निम्, अग्नौ, मध्यम् अग्नेः, वह्नौ, or चितायाम्, ‘to ascend the funeral pyre’; with कर्णयोः, ‘to come into the ears i.e. be heard’; with आत्मनि, or चित्तम्, ‘to take possession of the heart’; in dram. ‘to enter the stage’);
to reach, attain, Sarvad.;
to have sexual intercourse with (acc., applied to both sexes), MBh.; Suśr.;
to enter upon, undertake, commence, begin, devote one's self to (acc., rarely loc.), MBh.; Hariv.; R. &c. (with पिण्डीम् or तर्पणम्, ‘to accept or enjoy an oblation’);
to enter into i.e. be absorbed or thrown into the shade by (acc.), Hariv. (with [स्वानि] अङ्गानि or गात्राणि), ‘to shrink, shrivel’, R.; Kathās. :
Caus. -वेशयति, ˚ते, to cause or allow to enter, bring or lead or introduce to, usher into (acc. or loc.), AV. &c. &c. (without an object, ‘to bring into one's house &c.’, esp. ‘to bring on the stage’);
to lead home as a wife i.e. marry, MBh.;
to lay or store up, deposit in, put or throw into (loc. or acc.), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to enter i.e. commit to paper, write down, Yājñ., Sch.;
to initiate into (acc.), Prab.;
to instil into (loc.) = teach, impart, Kathās.;
to spend (money), Pañcat.;
to enter, come or be brought into (acc.), Var.; BhP. :
Desid. -विविक्षति, to wish to enter into (acc.), MBh.; R.

प्र-√ वी P. -वेति, to go forth, RV.;
to strive after, make for, enter into, ib.;
to attack, assail, ib.;
to enter, fertilize, impregnate, ib.; TS.; AV.; Kāṭh.;
to urge on, inspirit, animate, RV.

प्र-√ 2. वृ P. Ā. -वृणाति, (Ved.) -वृणीते; -वृणोति, -वृणुते (3. sg. aor. Subj. -वृत, RV.), to choose out, choose as (acc.) or for (dat.), RV.; Br.; MBh.; BhP.;
to accept gladly, RV. ix, 101, 13 :
Caus. -वरयति, to choose, select, MBh.;
-वारयति, to please, gratify, R. (For 1. प्रवर, mfn. best, &c., see p. 690, col. 3.)

प्रा-√ वृ 1. √ (प्रा prob. for प्र; cf. अपा-√ वृ) P. Ā. -वृणोति, -वृणुते (inf. -वरितुम्, Mṛcch.),
to cover, veil, conceal, AV.; Gaut.; Āpast.;
to put on, dress one's self in (acc., rarely instr.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to fill, MBh.

प्र-√ वृज् P. Ā. -वृणक्ति, -वृङ्क्ते, (Ved. inf. -वृ॑जे), to strew (the sacrificial grass), RV.; Br.;
to place in or on the fire, heat, ib.;
to perform the Pravargya ceremony, Br.; KātyŚr.

प्र-√ वृत् Ā. -वर्तते, (ep. also P. ˚ति), to roll or go onwards (as a carriage), be set in motion or going, ChUp.; MBh. &c.;
to set out, depart, betake one's self, MBh.; R. &c.;
to proceed (वर्त्मना, or ˚नि, on a path; अपथेन, on a wrong path), Kāv.; Kathās.;
to come forth, issue, originate, arise, be produced, result, occur, happen, take place, VS.; Br.; MBh. &c.;
to commence, begin to (inf.), set about, engage in, be intent upon or occupied with (dat. loc., or अर्थम् ifc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to proceed against, do injury to (loc.), MBh.; R.; Ragh. ;
to debauch (अन्यो ऽन्यम्, ‘one another’), MBh.;
to act or proceed according to or with (instr. or abl.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to behave or conduct one's self towards, deal with (loc.), ib.;
to hold good, prevail, ib.;
to continue, keep on (pr.p.), Hariv.; Sarvad.;
to be, exist, MārkP.;
to serve for, conduce to (dat., or अर्थम् ifc.), Sarvad.;
to mean, be used in the sense of (loc.), ib.;
to let any one (gen.) have anything (acc.), MBh. :
Caus. -वर्तयति, to cause to turn or roll, set in motion, RV. &c. &c.;
to throw, hurl, pour forth, RV.; MaitrS.;
to send, Prab.;
to set on foot, circulate, diffuse, divulge, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to introduce, appoint, instal, ib.;
to produce, create, accomplish, devise, invent, perform, do, make, ib. (with सेतुम् to erect a dam; with व्ययकर्म, to effect expenditure; with लोक-यात्राम्, to transact the business of life; with कथाम्, to relate a story);
to exhibit, show, display, R.; BhP.;
to undertake, begin, KātyŚr.; MBh. &c.;
to use, employ, Bhaṭṭ.;
to induce any one to do anything, betray into (loc.), Kathās.;
to proceed against (loc.), MBh.

प्र-√ वृध् P. -वर्धति, to exalt, magnify, RV. viii, 8, 22;
 Ā. -वर्धते (rarely P. ˚ति), to grow up, grow, increase, gain in strength, prosper, thrive, RV. &c. &c.:
Caus. -वर्धयति, ˚ते, to strengthen, increase, augment, extend, RV. &c. &c.;
to raise, exalt, cause to thrive, Hariv.;
to rear, cherish, bring up, Kathās.

प्र-√ व्यथ् Ā. -व्यथते, (ep. also P. ˚ति), to tremble, be afraid of (gen.), be disquieted or distressed, MBh.; R. &c.;
 = Caus. R. :
Caus. -व्यथयति, to frighten, disquiet, distress, MBh.; R.; Hariv.

प्र-√ व्यध् P. -विध्यति, to hurl, cast, throw away or down, RV. &c. &c.;
to hurl missiles, shoot, AV.; ŚBr.;
to pierce, transfix, wound, MBh.; Suśr.

प्र-व्य्-आ-√ हृ P. -हरति, to utter forth, speak, MBh.; R.;
to utter inarticulate sounds, howl, yell, roar, ib. (v.l. प्रत्याह्रि);
to declare beforehand, foretell, predict, MW. :
Caus. -हारयति, to speak, MBh.

प्र-√ व्रज् P. -व्रजति, to go forth, proceed, depart from (abl.), set out for, go to (acc. loc. or dat.), ŚBr.; Up.; GṛŚrS.; MBh. &c.;
to leave home and wander forth as an ascetic mendicant, ŚrS.; Mn.; MBh. &c.;
 (with Jainas) to become a monk, HPariś. :
Caus. -व्राजयति (w.r. -व्रज्˚), to send into exile, banish from (abl.), MBh.; R. &c.;
to compel any one to wander forth as an ascetic mendicant or to become a monk, MBh.; HPariś.
